John Ball‚Äôs <strong data-start="64" data-end="85">Patom Theory (PT)</strong> aligns closely with your <strong data-start="111" data-end="155">RSVP (Relativistic Scalar‚ÄìVector Plenum)</strong> and <strong data-start="160" data-end="180">Simulated Agency</strong> frameworks on structural, epistemic, and dynamical levels, though the formalisms differ. Below is a detailed comparative analysis showing how PT maps into your architecture.</p>
<hr data-start="356" data-end="359">
<h2 data-start="361" data-end="429">1. Foundational Commonality: Pattern‚ÄìRecognition over Computation</h2>
<h3 data-start="431" data-end="447">Patom Theory</h3>
<p data-start="448" data-end="732">Ball explicitly rejects the computational metaphor (‚Äúthe brain as computer‚Äù) and instead posits the brain as a <strong data-start="559" data-end="592">pattern-recognition hierarchy</strong> built from <strong data-start="604" data-end="635">bidirectionally linked sets</strong> (‚Äúpatoms‚Äù). Meaning arises from recursive pattern-matching between top-down and bottom-up flows.</p>
<h3 data-start="734" data-end="761">RSVP / Simulated Agency</h3>
<p data-start="762" data-end="1113">Your frameworks also reject the computational metaphor. RSVP replaces discrete computation with <strong data-start="858" data-end="880">entropic recursion</strong>: scalar potential <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Œ¶</span></span></span></span>, vector flow <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4444em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span></span></span></span>, and entropy density <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span></span></span></span> evolve through continuous field equations. Cognition and cosmology both emerge from <strong data-start="1053" data-end="1088">recursive constraint relaxation</strong>, not computation per se.</p>
<p data-start="1115" data-end="1134"><strong data-start="1115" data-end="1134">Correspondence:</strong></p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="1135" data-end="1541" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="1135" data-end="1177"><tr data-start="1135" data-end="1177"><th data-start="1135" data-end="1150" data-col-size="sm">Patom Theory</th><th data-start="1150" data-end="1177" data-col-size="md">RSVP / Simulated Agency</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="1223" data-end="1541"><tr data-start="1223" data-end="1303"><td data-start="1223" data-end="1256" data-col-size="sm">Bidirectional pattern matching</td><td data-start="1256" data-end="1303" data-col-size="md">Bidirectional scalar‚Äìvector coupling (Œ¶‚Üîùíó)</td></tr><tr data-start="1304" data-end="1371"><td data-start="1304" data-end="1331" data-col-size="sm">Hierarchical linked sets</td><td data-start="1331" data-end="1371" data-col-size="md">Multiscale recursive tiling (TARTAN)</td></tr><tr data-start="1372" data-end="1466"><td data-start="1372" data-end="1402" data-col-size="sm">Recognition drives function</td><td data-start="1402" data-end="1466" data-col-size="md">Entropic smoothing / constraint satisfaction drives function</td></tr><tr data-start="1467" data-end="1541"><td data-start="1467" data-end="1498" data-col-size="sm">Meaning as attractor pattern</td><td data-start="1498" data-end="1541" data-col-size="md">Semantic manifold / coherence attractor</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12