<p data-start="1543" data-end="1649">Both assert that intelligence arises from recursive pattern coherence, not algorithmic sequence execution.</p>
<hr data-start="1651" data-end="1654">
<h2 data-start="1656" data-end="1723">2. Structural Isomorphism: Hierarchical Linking vs. Sheaf Gluing</h2>
<p data-start="1725" data-end="1947">PT‚Äôs ‚Äúhierarchical bidirectional linked sets‚Äù are essentially <strong data-start="1787" data-end="1826">graph-structured semantic manifolds</strong>‚Äîeach node representing a multimodal pattern, with links allowing convergence and divergence of meanings across contexts.</p>
<p data-start="1949" data-end="1980">In RSVP‚Äôs categorical language:</p>
<ul data-start="1981" data-end="2256">
<li data-start="1981" data-end="2078">
<p data-start="1983" data-end="2078">A <strong data-start="1985" data-end="1994">patom</strong> ‚âà a <strong data-start="1999" data-end="2016">local section</strong> (a patch of coherence) in a sheaf over a semantic base space.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2079" data-end="2177">
<p data-start="2081" data-end="2177">The <strong data-start="2085" data-end="2110">bidirectional linking</strong> ‚âà <strong data-start="2113" data-end="2149">restriction and gluing morphisms</strong> between overlapping charts.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2178" data-end="2256">
<p data-start="2180" data-end="2256"><strong data-start="2180" data-end="2201">Pattern hierarchy</strong> ‚âà <strong data-start="2204" data-end="2234">recursive cover refinement</strong> in the TARTAN tiling.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2258" data-end="2439">Thus, PT‚Äôs storage and retrieval dynamics can be modeled as a <strong data-start="2320" data-end="2355">sheaf-theoretic entropic system</strong>, where coherence corresponds to successful pattern recognition (low local entropy).</p>
<hr data-start="2441" data-end="2444">
<h2 data-start="2446" data-end="2523">3. Meaning First: Role &amp; Reference Grammar ‚Üî Semantic Projection Operators</h2>
<p data-start="2525" data-end="2719">Ball‚Äôs adoption of <strong data-start="2544" data-end="2578">Role &amp; Reference Grammar (RRG)</strong> emphasizes that language is organized by <strong data-start="2620" data-end="2650">meaning and role structure</strong>, not syntax. Syntax emerges from semantic and pragmatic constraints.</p>
<p data-start="2721" data-end="3006">RSVP likewise defines <strong data-start="2743" data-end="2767">projection operators</strong> that map scalar (semantic potential) into vectorial (syntactic or behavioral) expressions under entropy constraints.<br data-start="2884" data-end="2887">
In <em data-start="2890" data-end="2908">Simulated Agency</em>, you formalize this as <strong data-start="2932" data-end="2976">semantic projection and sparse inference</strong>, where meaning precedes form.</p>
<p data-start="3008" data-end="3021"><strong data-start="3008" data-end="3021">Parallel:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3022" data-end="3309">
<li data-start="3022" data-end="3120">
<p data-start="3024" data-end="3120">RRG‚Äôs ‚ÄúActor‚ÄìUndergoer‚Äù roles correspond to <strong data-start="3068" data-end="3094">vector flow directions</strong> (source vs sink) in RSVP.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3121" data-end="3231">
<p data-start="3123" data-end="3231">PT‚Äôs meaning-driven parsing corresponds to <strong data-start="3166" data-end="3199">entropy-minimizing projection</strong> in your Simulated Agency model.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3232" data-end="3309">
<p data-start="3234" data-end="3309">Both reject syntax-first NLP; both insist on <strong data-start="3279" data-end="3308">semantics-first causation</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3311" data-end="3314">
<h2 data-start="3316" data-end="3388">4. Neuro-Field Mapping: PT‚Äôs Brain Regions ‚Üî RSVP‚Äôs Functional Fields</h2>
<p data-start="3390" data-end="3706">PT identifies the <strong data-start="3408" data-end="3449">posterior middle temporal gyrus (MTG)</strong> as the hub of word-to-meaning mapping and <strong data-start="3492" data-end="3508">Broca‚Äôs area</strong> for meaning-to-syntax generation.<br data-start="3542" data-end="3545">
You generalize this idea: cognition operates via <strong data-start="3594" data-end="3627">scalar‚Äìvector entropic fields</strong> linking perception (posterior) and action (anterior). In your field formalism:</p>
