<p data-start="3807" data-end="3950">mirrors the <strong data-start="3819" data-end="3852">top-down / bottom-up coupling</strong> Ball describes‚Äîwhere comprehension and generation are inverses within a shared entropic manifold.</p>
<p data-start="3952" data-end="4085">So PT‚Äôs localized cortical hierarchy can be viewed as a <strong data-start="4008" data-end="4044">finite biological implementation</strong> of RSVP‚Äôs continuous entropic recursion.</p>
<hr data-start="4087" data-end="4090">
<h2 data-start="4092" data-end="4169">5. Epistemological Convergence: ‚ÄúWhat the Brain Does‚Äù vs. ‚ÄúHow It Does It‚Äù</h2>
<p data-start="4171" data-end="4538">Ball writes that PT ‚Äúexplains what a brain does, not how it does it.‚Äù<br data-start="4240" data-end="4243">
Your RSVP and Simulated Agency theories also distinguish <strong data-start="4300" data-end="4325">functional invariants</strong> (recursive solvability, entropy reabsorption) from <strong data-start="4377" data-end="4403">mechanistic substrates</strong> (neural tissue, silicon, cosmological fields). Both treat intelligence as <strong data-start="4478" data-end="4500">a process category</strong> rather than a material configuration.</p>
<p data-start="4540" data-end="4697">This makes PT a <strong data-start="4556" data-end="4580">special case of RSVP</strong>‚Äîa cognitive-level instantiation of the same recursive informational physics you extend to cosmology and computation.</p>
<hr data-start="4699" data-end="4702">
<h2 data-start="4704" data-end="4731">6. Integrative Synthesis</h2>
