John Ball‚Äôs </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{Patom Theory} (PT) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{ball2020patom} offers a pattern‚Äìrecognition model of the brain that
complements the continuous field dynamics of the Relativistic Scalar--Vector Plenum (RSVP).  
Where RSVP formalizes cognition as recursive entropic flow among scalar capacity~</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
vector motion~</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and entropy density~</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(S)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, Patom Theory discretizes this recursion
into hierarchical, bidirectionally linked sets of patterns---</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{patoms}---that store and match meaning
both top--down and bottom--up.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Structural Correspondence.}
Each patom behaves as a local section in the RSVP manifold:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\longleftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>
(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i, S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
linked bidirectionally to its neighbors via restriction and gluing morphisms
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span>:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
The resulting hierarchy of linked sets is isomorphic to the RSVP sheaf structure,
where local coherence conditions define meaning and global sections correspond to
stable cognitive states (semantic attractors).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Dynamic Equivalence.}
Ball‚Äôs recognition algorithm---simultaneous top--down expectation and bottom--up confirmation---
corresponds to the RSVP recursion
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> t} = -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v} + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> S}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> t} = -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> enforces layered agreement between predicted and perceived
configurations.
Successful recognition in PT therefore represents a local minimum of entropic
discrepancy:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>S </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> 0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
yielding a coherent semantic projection.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Linguistic Realization.}
When coupled with Role and Reference Grammar (RRG),
PT models language generation and understanding as
bidirectional mappings between meaning and syntax.
Within RSVP, this process is captured by a
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{projection operator} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> acting on semantic potentials:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{syntax}}
  = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{sem}},S],
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
which mirrors the RRG transformation from semantic roles (Actor--Undergoer)
to syntactic structure.
Hence, Ball‚Äôs meaning-first linguistics
constitutes a discretized instantiation of RSVP‚Äôs entropic projection mechanism.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Neuro‚ÄìField Mapping.}
PT locates comprehension around the posterior middle temporal gyrus (MTG)
and generation near Broca‚Äôs area.
RSVP interprets this separation as a reciprocal flow of
scalar and vector potentials between perceptual and motor manifolds:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{MTG}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Broca}},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
realizing top--down semantic constraint and bottom--up articulatory enactment
within a single entropic field.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Synthesis.}
Patom Theory thus operationalizes RSVP at the cognitive scale:
a finite biological lattice sampling the continuous
plenum of entropic recursion.
Its hierarchical pattern architecture corresponds to
TARTAN‚Äôs recursive tiling,
its semantic coherence to Yarncrawler‚Äôs Markov‚Äìblanket stability,
and its recognition dynamics to Simulated Agency‚Äôs sparse inference.
In short, PT provides an empirical midpoint between
RSVP‚Äôs cosmological formalism and observable neurocognitive function,
demonstrating that meaning‚Äînot computation‚Äîis the fundamental invariant
across scales of mind and matter.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
