Your RSVP replaces computation with <strong data-start="626" data-end="659">recursive entropic relaxation</strong> among scalar (Œ¶), vector (ùíó), and entropy (S) fields.<br data-start="714" data-end="717">
‚Üí Both models treat cognition as <strong data-start="750" data-end="779">constraint reconciliation</strong> between top-down predictions and bottom-up confirmations‚Äîcontinuous in RSVP, discrete in PT.</p>
<hr data-start="874" data-end="877">
<h3 data-start="879" data-end="925">2. Formal Mapping: Patoms ‚Üî Sheaf Sections</h3>
<p data-start="926" data-end="1315">Each ‚Äúpatom‚Äù stores a multimodal invariant that can be linked upward and downward.<br data-start="1008" data-end="1011">
In RSVP terms, this is equivalent to a <strong data-start="1050" data-end="1067">local section</strong> in a <strong data-start="1073" data-end="1095">sheaf of coherence</strong> over the semantic base space, with restriction and gluing morphisms enforcing layered agreement.<br data-start="1192" data-end="1195">
PT‚Äôs ‚Äúlayered agreement‚Äù corresponds to your <strong data-start="1240" data-end="1271">entropic smoothing operator</strong> that drives Œ¶‚Äìùíó coupling toward minimal S.</p>
<hr data-start="1317" data-end="1320">
<h3 data-start="1322" data-end="1390">3. Linguistic Correspondence: RRG ‚Üî Semantic Projection Operator</h3>
<p data-start="1391" data-end="1656">Ball‚Äôs integration of PT with <strong data-start="1421" data-end="1457">Role and Reference Grammar (RRG)</strong> makes meaning‚Äînot syntax‚Äîthe primary driver of language.<br data-start="1514" data-end="1517">
In RSVP/Simulated Agency, your <strong data-start="1548" data-end="1572">projection functor ‚Ñõ</strong> maps semantic potentials (Œ¶) into syntactic vectors (ùíó) under entropy constraints:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mtext>syntax</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">R</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi><mtext>sem</mtext></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{\text{syntax}} = \mathcal{R}[\Phi_{\text{sem}},S],</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7305em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.016em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">syntax</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">R</span><span class="mopen">[</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">Œ¶</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">sem</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">‚Äã</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">]</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1726" data-end="1902">precisely mirroring RRG‚Äôs mapping from semantic roles to syntactic realizations.<br data-start="1806" data-end="1809">
Thus, RRG + PT instantiate your <strong data-start="1841" data-end="1858">meaning-first</strong> architecture at the human linguistic scale.</p>
<hr data-start="1904" data-end="1907">
<h3 data-start="1909" data-end="1937">4. Neuro-Field Parallels</h3>
