><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="491">Excellent‚Äîderiving <strong data-start="19" data-end="40">Patom Theory (PT)</strong> from the <strong data-start="50" data-end="94">Relativistic Scalar‚ÄìVector Plenum (RSVP)</strong> is a natural move: it establishes PT as the <em data-start="139" data-end="165">cognitive discretization</em> of RSVP‚Äôs continuous entropic recursion, rather than an independent brain model.<br data-start="246" data-end="249">
Below is a detailed academic <strong data-start="278" data-end="289">outline</strong> for an essay (or paper) that performs this derivation. It is structured for integration with your RSVP corpus and written to support inclusion in your <em data-start="441" data-end="459">Simulated Agency</em> or <em data-start="463" data-end="476">Yarncrawler</em> manuscripts.</p>
<hr data-start="493" data-end="496">
<h1 data-start="498" data-end="600"><strong data-start="500" data-end="600">Outline: From Plenum to Pattern‚ÄîDeriving Patom Theory from the Relativistic Scalar‚ÄìVector Plenum</strong></h1>
<hr data-start="602" data-end="605">
<h2 data-start="607" data-end="622"><strong data-start="610" data-end="622">Abstract</strong></h2>
<p data-start="623" data-end="1228">Patom Theory (Ball, 2020) proposes that brains operate not by computation but by hierarchical bidirectional pattern recognition (‚Äúpatoms‚Äù).<br data-start="762" data-end="765">
This essay derives PT formally from the Relativistic Scalar‚ÄìVector Plenum (RSVP), showing that its discrete linked-set architecture arises as a limiting case of RSVP‚Äôs continuous entropic recursion.<br data-start="963" data-end="966">
By applying RSVP‚Äôs field equations, sheaf structure, and entropy minimization dynamics to cognitive manifolds, we demonstrate how PT‚Äôs recognition hierarchies, meaning-first linguistics, and RRG compatibility follow necessarily from the plenum‚Äôs causal geometry.</p>
<hr data-start="1230" data-end="1233">
<h2 data-start="1235" data-end="1293"><strong data-start="1238" data-end="1293">1. Introduction: Two Theories of the Same Recursion</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="1294" data-end="1600">
<li data-start="1294" data-end="1363">
<p data-start="1296" data-end="1363">Context: The gap between computational AI and cognitive modeling.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1364" data-end="1431">
<p data-start="1366" data-end="1431">John Ball‚Äôs motivation: replacing computation with recognition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1432" data-end="1491">
<p data-start="1434" data-end="1491">RSVP as a unifying field theory of entropy and meaning.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1492" data-end="1600">
<p data-start="1494" data-end="1600">Thesis: Patom Theory = RSVP restricted to finite cognitive manifolds under quantized semantic constraints.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1602" data-end="1605">
<h2 data-start="1607" data-end="1635"><strong data-start="1610" data-end="1635">2. The RSVP Framework</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="1636" data-end="1655">2.1 Core Fields</h3>
<p data-start="1656" data-end="1678">Define the RSVP triad:</p>
