Patom Theory (Ball, 2020) describes the brain as a hierarchical, bidirectionally linked network of pattern-atoms (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{patoms}) that recognize meaning through layered agreement rather than computation.  
This essay derives Patom Theory formally from the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{Relativistic Scalar‚ÄìVector Plenum} (RSVP), demonstrating that its discrete cognitive architecture emerges as a quantized limit of RSVP‚Äôs continuous entropic recursion among scalar capacity </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, vector flow </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and entropy density </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(S)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
Within the RSVP framework, recognition corresponds to the local minimization of entropy through bidirectional coupling between </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>; discretizing these flows yields the pattern-matching operations characteristic of Patom Theory.  
The Role and Reference Grammar (RRG) model of meaning-first language generation and comprehension is then shown to instantiate RSVP‚Äôs projection operator </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,S] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, mapping semantic potentials into syntactic realizations through entropy-preserving projection.  
At the neurocognitive level, the posterior middle temporal gyrus and Broca‚Äôs area function as complementary scalar‚Äìvector domains, forming a finite biological loop equivalent to RSVP‚Äôs entropic feedback equation.  
Thus, Patom Theory is not an alternative to RSVP but its cognitive discretization: a finite, neurosemantic realization of the universal recursive dynamics that govern meaning, recognition, and agency across all scales.
