The </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{Relativistic Scalar--Vector Plenum} (RSVP) provides the foundational ontology
from which cognitive, physical, and semantic phenomena are all derived.
At its core, RSVP rejects the notion of a static spacetime or a symbol-manipulating mind,
and instead describes reality as a dynamic continuum of recursive information flow.
Every process---from cosmic structure formation to linguistic comprehension---is
interpreted as an instance of entropic relaxation within an interacting triplet of fields:
a scalar capacity~</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, a vector flow~</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and an entropy density~</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(S)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Field Triplet and Governing Equations}
Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x},t)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denote the scalar potential of a region,
quantifying its capacity to sustain structured order,
and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x},t)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> represent the local vector flow of activity or inference.
Entropy density </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x},t)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> measures the degree of uncertainty or disorder
within that region.  
The evolution of these fields is governed by a hepatic operator
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> enforcing local conservation of coherence:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{align}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> t} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v} + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S), </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{eq:phi-evo}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>[4pt]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> S}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> t} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{eq:entropy-evo}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>[4pt]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S] </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> 0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{as} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> 0. </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{eq:hepatic}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{align}
Equations~</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eqref</span></span><span>{eq:phi-evo}--</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eqref</span></span><span>{eq:entropy-evo}
express the continuous coupling between potential, flow, and entropy.
When integrated over any domain </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the average hepatic flux tends toward
nonpositivity, implying that entropy is continually reabsorbed into structure---the
formal condition for persistence.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Entropic Recursion as Recognition}
The central insight of RSVP is that recognition and coherence are
thermodynamically identical.
Whenever a subsystem stabilizes its internal description of the environment,
it is effectively minimizing local entropy through reciprocal adjustment of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
Recognition, prediction, and adaptation are therefore special cases of
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{entropic recursion}:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>S </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> 0.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
This principle unifies perception and inference:
top--down flows of potential predict structure,
while bottom--up flows of activity confirm or correct it.
The bidirectional symmetry between these flows establishes the formal
ground of meaning within the plenum.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Semantic Manifold and Sheaf Structure}
Because coherence is always local,
the plenum decomposes into overlapping regions of partial order.
Each region </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> defines a local section </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i,S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
The ensemble of all such sections, with restriction maps on their overlaps,
forms a sheaf~</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{S}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> over the base space of phenomena.
A globally consistent interpretation---a stable state of mind, a physical equilibrium,
or a grammatical sentence---corresponds to a global section of this sheaf.
Failures of agreement between overlaps generate entropy and drive further recursion.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Projection and Agency}
Within cognitive systems, RSVP dynamics give rise to
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{projection operators} that translate scalar semantic potentials into
vectorial expressions of action or syntax:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{out}} = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,S].
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
This operator formalizes how meaning becomes behavior or language,
and its adjoint </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ast</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> lifts observations back into the scalar field.
Together they define the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{CLIO} functor
(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{Cognitive Loop via In--Situ Optimization}),
a categorical representation of bidirectional inference.
At equilibrium, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ast</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span> I</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
indicating successful recognition or understanding.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Cognitive and Physical Continuum}
RSVP therefore describes not a symbolic algorithm but a universal medium
in which perception, cognition, and physics are different resolutions of the same
recursive flow.
When discretized through biological or computational constraints,
its continuous fields yield finite recognition structures.
In the following section, we show that John~Ball‚Äôs Patom Theory
arises precisely from such a discretization:
a lattice approximation of the plenum‚Äôs entropic recursion,
where each node of the lattice---each </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{patom}---acts as a local section
in the RSVP sheaf of meaning.
