The continuous dynamics of the Relativistic Scalar--Vector Plenum (RSVP) describe cognition
and perception as smooth entropic recursions across a manifold of meaning.
However, no biological or artificial substrate can instantiate an infinite continuum.
Finite agents---neurons, linguistic tokens, or cognitive modules---must approximate these
continuous flows through discrete and bounded representations.
Patom Theory (PT) emerges precisely from this discretization:
a finite, hierarchical lattice of pattern--atoms (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{patoms}) that
sample, store, and match fragments of the continuous plenum.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Semantic Quantization of the RSVP Fields}
Let the RSVP manifold be partitioned into </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>N</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> overlapping regions
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i=1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>N</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, each characterized by locally coherent field values:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i, S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Each region </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> functions as a quantized packet of semantic coherence,
analogous to an elementary excitation in a physical field.
The corresponding discrete unit,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\equiv</span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i, S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
is a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{pattern--atom}, or </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{patom}, representing the smallest
recoverable unit of recognition.
Patoms are not static symbols but dynamic constraints: each stores the conditions under
which the surrounding plenum attains low entropy.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Bidirectional Coupling Between Patoms}
In the continuous RSVP framework, coherence is maintained through reciprocal flows
between scalar and vector fields.  Discretization replaces these fields with
bidirectional links between neighboring patoms:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Longleftrightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\exists</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ji}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ such that }
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i,S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ji}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j,S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Here </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ji}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> act as restriction and gluing morphisms,
forming a discrete analogue of the sheaf structure introduced in
Section~</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ref</span></span><span>{eq:hepatic}.
When mutual consistency is achieved across all overlapping regions,
the network of patoms realizes a global section of the RSVP sheaf,
corresponding to a coherent perception or thought.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Layered Agreement as Discrete Entropic Equilibrium}
In the plenum, entropy gradients drive local flows until
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}} S </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span> 0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
In the discretized system, this same condition becomes a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{layered agreement} among patoms:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{j</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{N}(i)} S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> 0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{N}(i)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denotes the neighborhood of patom </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
Recognition occurs when the entropy difference between linked patoms vanishes to first order,
implying that top--down predictions and bottom--up confirmations coincide.
This reproduces Ball‚Äôs empirical finding that meaning, not form,
drives the stabilization of linguistic and perceptual recognition.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Hierarchical Organization}
Because each patom can itself serve as a component in higher--order patterns,
the discrete lattice forms a hierarchy:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subset</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subset</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdots</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subset</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> represents the </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>--th level of aggregation or abstraction.
Lower layers encode sensory or phonetic features; higher layers encode conceptual,
pragmatic, or discourse structures.
This recursive composability corresponds to the multi--scale tiling of RSVP‚Äôs
TARTAN architecture and provides the structural basis for semantic generalization.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{From Flows to Links: The Discretization Limit}
The transition from the continuous RSVP dynamics to the discrete PT hierarchy
can be understood formally as a sampling of the plenum at finite resolution </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lim</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> x </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> 0} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> x)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>
(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> S(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i)).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
At this limit, the network of patoms converges to the continuous plenum.
Conversely, any finite neural or computational realization must operate at
nonzero </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, producing a recognizable but lossy discretization.
Hence Patom Theory does not contradict RSVP; it approximates it under finite
perceptual and energetic constraints.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Recognition as Discrete Entropic Minimization}
Each recognition event in Patom Theory corresponds to the minimization of
a local discrete entropy functional:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{E} = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>(S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\bar</span></span><span>{S}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{N}(i)}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{E}}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i} = 0
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Longleftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>
S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\bar</span></span><span>{S}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{N}(i)}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
This discrete entropic equilibrium condition parallels the RSVP variational
principle and provides a direct mathematical bridge between continuous
entropic recursion and the pattern--matching algorithm of PT.
Through this correspondence, hierarchical recognition can be seen as a
finite--resolution implementation of the universal plenum dynamics.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
