01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>*{Appendix C: Experimental Protocols and Practical Measurements}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{C.1 Overview and Hypotheses}
We operationalize RSVP‚ÄìCLIO recognition dynamics via three complementary streams:
(1) neural oscillations (EEG/MEG), (2) hemodynamics (fMRI), and (3) algorithmic
telemetry from CLIO loops in LLMs. Our primary hypotheses are:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{H1 (Recognition oscillations):} During recognition (not mere prediction),
theta--gamma cross-frequency coupling (CFC) increases over posterior (MTG/AG) and
fronto-motor (Broca/SMA) networks; torsion energy </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> decreases.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{H2 (Entropy descent):} Proxy entropy </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> S(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> monotonically decreases
(or exhibits underdamped oscillations) until stabilization at recognition equilibrium.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{H3 (Tri-modal alignment):} Peaks and phase-resets in CLIO uncertainty
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> U(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> align with neural phase-rests (theta) and transient increases in BOLD entropy,
then jointly settle as recognition is achieved.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

Throughout, we track:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}(t) := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tfrac</span></span><span>{1}{2}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v} - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 d</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
U(t) := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Big</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,S]</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span> (S-S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ast</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Big</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> d</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{C.2 EEG/MEG: Cross-Frequency Coupling (CFC) Protocol}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Participants and Tasks.}
Healthy adults (N=30--40). Within-subject, counterbalanced tasks:
(1) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Recognition-first}: speeded semantic match (picture/word) with re-encountered patterns;
(2) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Prediction-first control}: syntax-completion with low semantic load; 
(3) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Ambiguity resolution}: garden-path sentences or semantic illusions.
Each trial marks: stimulus onset, disambiguation point, recognition button.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Acquisition and Preprocessing.}
EEG: 64--128 channels (1,000 Hz); MEG: whole-head (1,200 Hz). Band-pass 1--150 Hz; notch line noise; ICA artifact correction. Source reconstruction to MTG/AG (posterior) and IFG/BA44/45/SMA (anterior).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{CFC Metrics.}
Compute per region (and inter-region) for sliding windows (e.g., 500 ms, 50</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\%</span></span><span> overlap):

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Phase--Amplitude Coupling (PAC):} Modulation Index (MI) via Tort or Canolty method between theta (4--8 Hz) phase and gamma (30--80 Hz) amplitude. 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Phase--Phase Coupling (PPC):} Phase-Locking Value (PLV) and debiased wPLI for theta/theta and theta/gamma edges across sources.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Cross-bispectrum:} Normalized bicoherence to detect quadratic phase coupling around (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Recognition/Torsion Indices.}
Define a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{neural torsion proxy}:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{EEG/MEG}}(t) := 1 - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{PLV}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{MTG}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{IFG})
+ </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{CFD}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{MTG},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{IFG}),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\overline</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{PLV}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> is mean theta PLV (higher </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Rightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> lower torsion),
and </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{CFD}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> is cross-frequency desynchrony (higher </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Rightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> higher torsion).
Set </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> to scale (e.g., 0.3).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Expected Signatures.}
H1 predicts PAC(Œ∏‚ÜíŒ≥) rise and PLV</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> increase at recognition; 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{EEG/MEG}}(t)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> decreases with underdamped oscillations (Q-factor 1.5--3.0)
that settle at response.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Statistics and Power.}
Within-subject mixed models on MI/PLV peaks aligned to response. Cluster-based permutation tests
for time‚Äìfrequency contrasts (recognition vs prediction). Power: effects </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>d</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span> 0.6</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> detectable with </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>N</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> 28</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{C.3 fMRI: Entropy Proxies and Dynamic Connectivity}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Acquisition.}
3T/7T multiband EPI (TR 600‚Äì800 ms), whole-brain. Task blocks synchronized with EEG/MEG sessions in a subset (N=20) or separate cohort (N=30).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Preprocessing.}
Standard fMRIPrep; nuisance regression; temporal filtering (0.008‚Äì0.25 Hz). Parcellation (e.g., Schaefer-400) with explicit ROIs (MTG/AG/IFG/SMA/hippocampus/MD thalamus/cerebellum).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Entropy Proxies </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{BOLD}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>.}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Sample Entropy (SampEn)} and </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Permutation Entropy} per ROI time series.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Lempel‚ÄìZiv Complexity (LZc)} on binarized BOLD.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Graph Entropy:} Shannon entropy of time-resolved connectivity graphs; 
and </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{von Neumann entropy} using Laplacian spectrum.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{HMM State Entropy:} entropy over latent state occupancy in dynamic FC HMMs.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{RSVP Mapping.}
Treat </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{BOLD}}(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> as a hemodynamic proxy of </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> S(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>.
Define fMRI torsion proxy via asymmetry in directed connectivity:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{fMRI}}(t) := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{1}{E}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{(i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> j)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> E}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>| </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{GC}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> j}(t) - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{GC}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{j</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> i}(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span>|,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
with sliding-window Granger (or spectral DCM parameters). Recognition predicts
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{BOLD}}(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\downarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{fMRI}}(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\downarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>,
coincident with EEG/MEG CFC stabilization.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Joint Inference.}
Cross-modal alignment: compute cross-correlations between </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{BOLD}}(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>,
PAC(Œ∏‚ÜíŒ≥), and behavioral RT. Expect negative correlation between PAC peak latency and final </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{BOLD}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{C.4 CLIO Telemetry for LLMs: Uncertainty and Torsion Observables}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Instrumentation.}
At each CLIO pass </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>, log:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{e}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k - S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ast</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{e}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k,S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k]</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
plus: plan graph size, belief entropy (Shannon over candidate nodes), self-reported confidence,
and step time. If available, log an </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{algorithmic torsion}:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{alg}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{curl}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2
- 2</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k , </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
using discrete analogues (finite differences on token-time grid).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Oscillation Detection and Q-Factor.}
Fit </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> with a damped sinusoid </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span> A e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\zeta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\omega</span></span><span> k}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cos</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\omega</span></span><span> k + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span>)+C</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>.
Estimate </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>Q </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tfrac</span></span><span>{1}{2</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\zeta</span></span><span>}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>. Recognition corresponds to </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span>[1,3]</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> with </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> C</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>.
Flag non-convergent loops if </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>Q&gt;4</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> or </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> trend increases.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Triggers for In-Situ Intervention.}
If </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k &gt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>U </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> or phase slip detected (instantaneous frequency jump),
invoke: (i) graph pruning, (ii) strategy re-formulation, (iii) external query.
These correspond to hepatic corrections in RSVP.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Alignment With Human Data.}
Time-lock CLIO </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> peaks to EEG theta phase resets and to fMRI dynamic state transitions.
Hypothesis H3 predicts tight alignment (jitter </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>&lt;200</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> ms in EEG/MEG; </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>&lt;</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> 1 TR in fMRI).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{C.5 Analysis Plan and Pre-registration Elements}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Primary Outcomes.}
PAC(Œ∏‚ÜíŒ≥) peak height/latency, PLV</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{BOLD}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{EEG/MEG}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{fMRI}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>, CLIO </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> damping ratio </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\zeta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Confirmatory Tests.}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Recognition vs prediction: higher PAC, lower torsion proxies, faster </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> damping.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Ambiguity trials: larger initial </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>, greater oscillation amplitude, but same asymptote.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Cross-modal synchrony: maximal PAC growth rate coincides with largest negative derivative of </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{BOLD}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Exploratory Analyses.}
Cross-bispectrum topographies; directed connectivity (DCM) changes as a function of </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>; 
individual differences (working memory span) as moderators.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Sample Size Guidance.}
EEG/MEG: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>N</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span> 32</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> for PAC effect </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>d=0.6</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> (power 0.8, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>=0.05</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>); 
fMRI: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>N</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span> 30</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> for medium graph-entropy effects (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>d=0.5</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>); 
Tri-modal sub-cohort </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>N=20</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> acceptable with within-subject designs.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{C.6 Implementation Notes and Pitfalls}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{CFC Pitfalls:} control for non-sinusoidal waveform confounds (harmonics).
Use surrogate data and cycle-shuffling to validate PAC.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Source Leakage:} apply leakage-reduction (SSBL/LCMV orthogonalization) before inter-ROI PLV/wPLI.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{fMRI Entropy Bias:} normalize entropy by surrogate autoregressive nulls; avoid TR-driven artifacts.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Telemetry Calibration:} ensure consistent definitions of </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> across CLIO variants; 
stabilize </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>, step sizes to avoid spurious over-damping.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{C.7 Integration Rule (Tri-Modal)}
Define a composite recognition score per trial:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{RecScore} := z</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\left</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{PAC}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\right</span></span><span>)
- z</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\left</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\min</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{EEG/MEG}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\right</span></span><span>)
- z</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\left</span></span><span>(S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{BOLD}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{end}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\right</span></span><span>)
- z</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\left</span></span><span>(U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>K</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\right</span></span><span>),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>z(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> z-scoring across trials and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>K</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> the final CLIO uncertainty.
Higher </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{RecScore}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> indicates stronger, faster recognition consistent with RSVP.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{C.8 Expected Outcomes and Falsifiability}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Support for RSVP‚ÄìCLIO:} monotone (or underdamped) descent in </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U(t)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}(t)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>,
coincident PAC increases, and decreasing BOLD entropy at recognition.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Falsification:} if recognition occurs without any PAC/PLV change, without </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>U(t)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> damping,
or with increasing torsion proxies, the recognition-first account is challenged and requires
revising the hepatic operator or projection model.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
