rd talk you dropped in? Here‚Äôs the crisp version.
 
# Executive summary
 
 
-  
**Thesis.** Today‚Äôs ‚Äúgenerative AI‚Äù is *unsustainable* (energy, cost, reliability) and structurally ill-suited to true language understanding. The proposed successor is **Cognitive AI**, built from **brain science + linguistics** (specifically, Role &amp; Reference Grammar, RRG) rather than big statistics alone.  
 
 
-  
**Core claim.** Cognitive AI separates **linguistic skill** (mapping words‚Üímeaning) from **world knowledge** (context, facts), aiming to eliminate combinatorial blow-ups and reduce hallucinations. Predicates ‚Äúdetermine their arguments,‚Äù constraining what can sensibly combine. 
 
 
-  
**Why now / ‚Äúcrisis.‚Äù** Generative AI overpromises (robots, universal AGI) yet still fails at robust understanding; governments and tech giants are pouring money into energy-hungry data centers‚Äîseen here as the wrong path.  
 
 

 
# What the demo showed
 
 
-  
**Context tracking &amp; Q/A.** Add entities to context and the system answers ‚ÄúWho arrived?‚Äù correctly as context evolves (Beth ‚Üí Beth &amp; John ‚Üí Beth, John, Sue, Dana), and handles tense/pronominal answers (‚ÄúShe did,‚Äù ‚ÄúHe did‚Äù). 
 
 
-  
**Meaning generalization.** From specific events (‚ÄúJohn ate cereal‚Äù) the system answers passives (‚ÄúWho was the cereal eaten by?‚Äù), multi-wh questions (‚ÄúWho ate what?‚Äù), and contrasts (‚ÄúDid Sue eat the cereal? ‚Äî No, John did‚Äù). 
 
 
-  
**Ambiguity &amp; prepositions.** Location/state depends on meaning (‚Äúat the beach,‚Äù ‚Äúon the mat,‚Äù ‚Äúin the kitchen‚Äù)‚Äînot mere word patterns. 
 
 
-  
**Nominalizations &amp; event structure.** From ‚Äúthe destruction of the city by the vandals,‚Äù it still recovers **who destroyed what** via predicate meaning (destruction ‚Üî destroy). 
 
 

 
# The linguistic engine (RRG) in a nutshell
 
 
-  
Move from **triples** and parts-of-speech-first parsing to **meaning representations** where predicates have 0/1/2/3+ arguments, causal structure, and event/state transformations (e.g., *die* = ‚Äúbecome dead‚Äù; *kill* = ‚Äúcause(become dead)‚Äù). This supports principled generalization and cleaner knowledge graphs.  
 
 
-  
RRG + semiotics: map **form ‚Üí meaning ‚Üí interpretation in context**, not just syntax trees. 
 
 

 
# Engineering posture
 
 
-  
Treat meanings as **typed predicates + roles**; build a **tested repository** per language (unit &amp; integration tests) so new vocabulary can be added without regressions. Aim for deterministic, transparent behavior. 
 
 

 
# Where they want this used
 
 
-  
**Enterprise assistants** (deterministic, auditable language understanding) and **language learning** (brain-inspired ‚Äúbrain soaking‚Äù &amp; ‚Äúface phonics‚Äù for easier L2 acquisition).  
 
 

 
# Why it matters (according to the talk)
 
 
-  
**Sustainability.** Reduce dependence on giant pattern-matching stacks; do more with meaning + context rather than brute force compute. 
 
 
-  
**Trust/controllability.** If the system always builds an explicit meaning structure, you can verify *why* an answer holds (and correct it) rather than shrugging at a latent vector.
 
 

  
If you want, I can convert this into:
 
 
1.  
a one-page brief for stakeholders, or
 
 
2.  
a side-by-side ‚ÄúCognitive AI vs. GenAI‚Äù checklist you can drop into your RSVP-TARTAN docs.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex justify-end"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none duration-300 group-hover/turn-messages:delay-300 pointer-events-none opacity-0 motion-safe:transition-opacity group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:opacity-100 group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:opacity-100 has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:opacity-100" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896 16.835 6.5 16.835H9.33301C10.0439 16.835 10.5374 16.8341 10.9209 16.8027C11.2965 16.772 11.508 16.7152 11.666 16.634