.6348 11.666L16.6914 11.5361C16.7428 11.3924 16.7797 11.2026 16.8027 10.9209C16.8341 10.5374 16.835 10.0439 16.835 9.33301V6.5C16.835 5.78896 16.8341 5.29563 16.8027 4.91211C16.7797 4.63025 16.7428 4.44063 16.6914 4.29688L16.6348 4.16699C16.4807 3.86474 16.2466 3.61186 15.959 3.43555L15.833 3.36524C15.675 3.28473 15.4636 3.22797 15.0879 3.19727C14.7044 3.16593 14.211 3.16504 13.5 3.16504H10.667C9.9561 3.16504 9.46259 3.16595 9.0791 3.19727C8.79739 3.22028 8.6076 3.2572 8.46387 3.30859L8.33399 3.36524C8.03176 3.51923 7.77886 3.75343 7.60254 4.04102L7.53125 4.16699C7.4508 4.32498 7.39397 4.53655 7.36328 4.91211C7.33985 5.19893 7.33562 5.54719 7.33399 6.00195H9.33301C10.022 6.00195 10.5791 6.00131 11.0293 6.03809C11.4873 6.07551 11.8937 6.15471 12.2705 6.34668L12.4883 6.46875C12.984 6.7728 13.3878 7.20854 13.6533 7.72949L13.7197 7.87207C13.8642 8.20859 13.9292 8.56974 13.9619 8.9707C13.9987 9.42092 13.998 9.97799 13.998 10.667V12.665ZM18.165 9.33301C18.165 10.022 18.1657 10.5791 18.1289 11.0293C18.0961 11.4302 18.0311 11.7914 17.8867 12.1279L17.8203 12.2705C17.5549 12.7914 17.1509 13.2272 16.6553 13.5313L16.4365 13.6533C16.0599 13.8452 15.6541 13.9245 15.1963 13.9619C14.8593 13.9895 14.4624 13.9935 13.9951 13.9951C13.9935 14.4624 13.9895 14.8593 13.9619 15.1963C13.9292 15.597 13.864 15.9576 13.7197 16.2939L13.6533 16.4365C13.3878 16.9576 12.9841 17.3941 12.4883 17.6982L12.2705 17.8203C11.8937 18.0123 11.4873 18.0915 11.0293 18.1289C10.5791 18.1657 10.022 18.165 9.33301 18.165H6.5C5.81091 18.165 5.25395 18.1657 4.80371 18.1289C4.40306 18.0962 4.04235 18.031 3.70606 17.8867L3.56348 17.8203C3.04244 17.5548 2.60585 17.151 2.30176 16.6553L2.17969 16.4365C1.98788 16.0599 1.90851 15.6541 1.87109 15.1963C1.83431 14.746 1.83496 14.1891 1.83496 13.5V10.667C1.83496 9.978 1.83432 9.42091 1.87109 8.9707C1.90851 8.5127 1.98772 8.10625 2.17969 7.72949L2.30176 7.51172C2.60586 7.0159 3.04236 6.6122 3.56348 6.34668L3.70606 6.28027C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Mathematical Correspondence Between RRG Logical Structures and RSVP Field Operators}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:RRG-math}

In Role and Reference Grammar (RRG), a sentence is represented as a logical
structure (LS) that decomposes events into predicates and their arguments.
For example, the transitive clause
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{John killed Mary}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
is represented as
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{do'}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{John}, [</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{kill'}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{John}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Mary})]),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
which expands further to
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{do'}(x, [</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{cause'}(x, [</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{become'}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{dead'}(y))])]).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
This notation captures causal and temporal dependencies, where the
outer predicate (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{do‚Ä≤}) introduces agency, and inner predicates
(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{cause‚Ä≤}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{become‚Ä≤}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{dead‚Ä≤}) define event transitions.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>*{Mapping Predicates to Scalar Potentials}
In RSVP, each predicate </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>P</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> defines a scalar potential </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> on a
semantic manifold </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x}) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{intensity of constraint imposed by } P</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Arguments correspond to coordinate axes or evaluation points
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> within </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, representing participants,
properties, or contextual bindings.  The semantic role assignment
(subject, object, oblique) defines the orientation of the local gradient
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, determining how meaning flows between
participants.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>*{Causal and Aspectual Operators as Field Derivatives}
RRG‚Äôs operators such as </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{do‚Ä≤}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{cause‚Ä≤}, and </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{become‚Ä≤}
introduce higher-order dynamics that correspond to temporal or causal
derivatives in RSVP:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{aligned}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{do'}(x,[P]) </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\longleftrightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{d</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>P}{dt}
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{(agent-driven change in potential)},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{cause'}(x,[P]) </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\longleftrightarrow</span></span><span> -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>x </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>P
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{(force applied along causal gradient)},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{become'}(P) </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\longleftrightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>P
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{(temporal evolution of a state predicate)},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{state'}(P) </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\longleftrightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>P = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{const.}
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{(equilibrium configuration)}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{aligned}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Thus, aspectual distinctions in RRG (achievement, accomplishment, activity,
state) correspond to the sign and curvature of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
governing whether the semantic field accelerates toward or away from
equilibrium.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>*{Vector Fields as Argument Flow}
For each predicate‚Äìargument pair </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(P</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, RSVP defines a
vector field </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> representing the direction and rate of
reference transfer:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij} = -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{x}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
These vectors encode the causal or thematic role structure (e.g., agent,
patient, instrument) as oriented flow lines in a shared semantic manifold.
The linking rules of RRG‚Äîdetermining which argument surfaces as subject or
object‚Äîcorrespond to boundary conditions on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> that preserve
global divergence-free coherence:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v} = 0
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Rightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{referential continuity across clauses}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>*{Clause Composition as Field Superposition}
When RRG composes multiple predicates (e.g., </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{cause‚Ä≤(become‚Ä≤(dead‚Ä≤(y)))})
the corresponding RSVP representation is a field superposition:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{composite}} =
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{cause}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\oplus</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{become}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\oplus</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{dead}},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{composite}} =
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Composition is associative because RSVP‚Äôs field addition is linear in the
potential‚Äìflow pair.  Nested logical structures yield hierarchical manifolds
in which outer predicates constrain the boundary conditions of inner fields.
For instance, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{John killed Mary} represents the imposition of
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{cause}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> on the transition </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{become}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> driving
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{dead}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, resulting in the global energy drop
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> S &lt; 0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>‚Äîthe informational signature of a completed recognition event.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>*{Discourse and Context as Boundary Conditions}
RRG‚Äôs discourse-level phenomena (focus, topic, anaphora) correspond to
global boundary constraints on the RSVP field domain </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
A discourse provides the large-scale potential surface within which local
predicational flows evolve:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span> = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{local}} + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{context}},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{n}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}|</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} = 0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
ensuring coherence across sentences and paragraphs just as physical fields
maintain smooth continuity across domain boundaries.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>*{Recognition as Torsion Minimization}
Finally, comprehension in RRG---the successful interpretation of a
predicate‚Äìargument configuration---occurs when all local torsions vanish:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{T} = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v} - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> = 0.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
This is the RSVP condition for complete recognition, equivalent to the
moment when the linguistic form, semantic meaning, and contextual
constraints align.  In this way, every well-understood sentence represents
a locally equilibrated region of the semantic plenum.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>*{Summary}
Through this mapping, RRG‚Äôs logical structures become local solutions of
the RSVP field equations:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
