w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="282">Understood ‚Äî here are three stylistically distinct <strong data-start="51" data-end="77">one-sentence epigraphs</strong> that could follow your conclusion, depending on the tone you want the essay to close on.<br data-start="166" data-end="169">
I‚Äôll show you options in increasing philosophical intensity, so you can pick or adapt the one that feels right.</p>
<hr data-start="284" data-end="287">
<p data-start="289" data-end="338"><strong data-start="289" data-end="336">1. Minimal and scientific (succinct close):</strong></p>
<blockquote data-start="339" data-end="419">
<p data-start="341" data-end="419"><em data-start="341" data-end="419">‚ÄúIntelligence is the steady state of recognition in a universe that learns.‚Äù</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="421" data-end="494"><strong data-start="421" data-end="492">2. Reflective and cosmological (mirrors RSVP‚Äôs entropic recursion):</strong></p>
<blockquote data-start="495" data-end="618">
<p data-start="497" data-end="618"><em data-start="497" data-end="618">‚ÄúThe universe does not compute‚Äîit recognizes, folding difference into coherence until meaning and matter are the same.‚Äù</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="620" data-end="683"><strong data-start="620" data-end="681">3. Poetic and humanistic (mirrors the essay‚Äôs moral arc):</strong></p>
<blockquote data-start="684" data-end="771">
<p data-start="686" data-end="771"><em data-start="686" data-end="771">‚ÄúEvery mind is the place where the cosmos pauses long enough to understand itself.‚Äù</em></p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="773" data-end="776">
