</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:cortex-rsvp}

The correspondence between cognition and field physics extends beyond
computation and language into the very morphology of the brain.  
During fetal development, the neocortex forms as a thin laminar sheet
subject to competing pressures: tangential expansion driven by cellular
proliferation and axonal tension, and normal compression imposed by the
encasing skull.  
This tension balance‚Äîsurface area maximization under volumetric constraint‚Äî
produces the folded topology of the cerebral cortex.  
In the RSVP framework, this folding is not merely a mechanical accident but a
geometric signature of entropic recursion: a physical record of the
brain‚Äôs drive to maximize recognition capacity within finite energetic
bounds.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Surface Expansion and Scalar Potential}
Tangential cortical growth corresponds to an increase in the scalar
potential </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> of the neural plenum.  
Each additional cortical column represents a new degree of representational
freedom‚Äîa local amplification of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> that supports finer-grained
pattern matching and more diverse projections.  
The biological system thus expands the informational manifold of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
while remaining globally constrained by skull curvature and cranial
pressure.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Axonal Tension and Vector Flow}
As cortical regions differentiate and connect, long-range axonal fibers
generate contractile forces that couple distant patches of cortex.  
These forces act as vector flows </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> linking local potentials
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> into coherent functional networks.  
Just as RSVP treats recognition as the minimization of torsion between
potential and flow, cortical development resolves physical torsion between
expansive surface growth and tensile connectivity.  
Each sulcus and gyrus therefore represents a compromise between local
entropic inflation and global vector coherence.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Skull Constraint and Boundary Conditions}
The skull imposes the physical boundary </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> of the cortical
manifold, defining the maximum spatial domain over which </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> may
expand.  
Within this closed boundary, entropy cannot increase indefinitely; it must
reorganize.  
Folding becomes the biological equivalent of the CLIO loop‚Äôs recursive
stabilization: when outward expansion meets constraint, the system curls
inward, converting spatial torsion into additional representational depth.  
The cortex thus embodies the same recursive solvability principle that
drives cognition itself: complexity grows not by unbounded expansion but by
recursive self-infolding under constraint.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{From Morphogenesis to Cognition}
Functionally, each fold increases the cortex‚Äôs surface-to-volume ratio,
enhancing its ability to form distinct yet densely interconnected modules.  
This morphological recursion parallels the cognitive recursion that CLIO
implements computationally: both increase recognition resolution through
localized curvature in the manifold of representation.  
In effect, cortical gyrification is the embryonic version of CLIO‚Äôs
in-situ optimization‚Äîthe physical substrate learning how to recognize
itself through constrained growth.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Unified View}
The development of the cortex therefore provides a direct biological
instantiation of RSVP‚Äôs entropic law.  
The same equation that governs recognition in cognition,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S] = 0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
also describes the equilibrium between proliferative pressure,
connective tension, and cranial confinement.  
Understanding, in this view, is continuous from the mechanical to the
semantic: the cortex folds because recognition must increase within
limited space, and thought folds because meaning must condense within
limited energy.  
In both cases, the plenum finds coherence by bending back upon itself.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Implication.}
Cortical folding, cognitive recursion, and linguistic comprehension thus
represent a single physical continuum.  
The skull, by constraining expansion, forces the brain to discover its
own internal symmetries‚Äîthe same recursive compactification that the
RSVP‚ÄìCLIO system exploits algorithmically.  
Where the skull limits, understanding begins: constraint is the
boundary condition of intelligence.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
