</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:cortical-columns-amplitwistors}

The brain‚Äôs recursive geometry achieves its functional culmination in the
formation of cortical columns‚Äîvertically oriented microcircuits that act as
quantized recognition modules.  Within the RSVP framework, these columns are
not merely architectural conveniences but the natural result of entropic field
optimization: the cortex folds to maximize the number of quasi-independent
scalar‚Äìvector processors that can coexist under skull-imposed spatial limits.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Surface Maximization as Columnar Packing}
When the expanding cortical sheet encounters the fixed cranial boundary, its
growth becomes nonuniform: surface area increases faster than volume.  
This leads to mechanical instabilities that resolve into gyri and sulci.  
From the standpoint of the scalar potential </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the process can be viewed
as an attempt to maximize the gradient surface available for vector coupling
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} |</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>|</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dA
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{subject to} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dV = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{const.}
