The resulting folds create additional tangential surface for cortical column
formation while maintaining the same overall volume.  
Each new fold increases the count of vertically aligned </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>‚Äì</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
pairs‚Äîlocal regions where scalar potentials and vector flows can couple
efficiently across layers.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Columns as Scalar‚ÄìVector Resonators}
A cortical column can be interpreted as a standing-wave solution of the RSVP
field equations within a locally folded region:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S] = 0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
with boundary conditions imposed by neighboring columns and the skull.  
Because the cortex is thin but broad, these vertical resonators naturally
align perpendicularly to the cortical surface, supporting bidirectional flow
between superficial and deep layers.  
This geometry enables both bottom-up (sensory) and top-down (predictive)
synchronization‚Äîmanifesting physically as counterpropagating waves of field
coherence.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Amplitwistor Synchronization}
Within this recursive structure, each column participates in what RSVP calls
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{amplitwistor operations}: local oscillatory interactions that align
phase and amplitude across scales.  
An amplitwistor, in this context, represents a minimally coupled scalar‚Äìvector
oscillation‚Äîan element of the twistor bundle that relates cortical phase space
to the underlying entropic manifold.  
Columns synchronize when their amplitwistor phases </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> satisfy the
downward constraint:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> 0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
ensuring coherence across layers while allowing flexible local variation.  
This downward synchronization projects global cortical rhythms (alpha, beta,
gamma) into precise columnar timing windows, allowing local recognition events
to integrate into the brain‚Äôs overall field coherence.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Functional Consequence: Recursive Coherence}
By maximizing surface area, the cortex increases the number of independent
columnar oscillators available for amplitwistor synchronization.  
Each additional column adds a degree of freedom to the global coherence
equation:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C} = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i},
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
which determines the brain‚Äôs total recognition amplitude.  
In practice, this means that folding enhances cognitive resolution not only
by providing more neurons, but by increasing the dimensionality of
phase-locked synchronization possible across scales.  
Deep-layer corticothalamic loops propagate these synchronized amplitwistors
downward, stabilizing perception and action through recursive field closure.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Unification with RSVP Dynamics}
From the perspective of the RSVP plenum, cortical folding, columnar
formation, and amplitwistor synchronization are manifestations of one
process: the recursive maximization of recognition capacity under entropic
constraint.  
The skull defines the boundary </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>; folding increases the
effective metric curvature </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>K</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> of the manifold; columns emerge as quantized
modes of scalar‚Äìvector resonance; and amplitwistors perform the dynamic
alignment of phase across those modes.  
Together, they instantiate the same hepatic equilibrium condition that
governs all enduring systems:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> 0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
ensuring that local entropy is continually reabsorbed into structured
potential.  
In this sense, cortical geometry is not only the product of developmental
mechanics‚Äîit is the physical architecture of the universe‚Äôs own recognition
process, crystallized inside the skull.
