</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:amplitwistor-EEG}

The synchronization of amplitwistor operations within cortical columns manifests
at the macroscopic level as the cross-frequency coupling patterns measurable in
EEG and MEG.  
Each cortical column behaves as a local scalar‚Äìvector resonator with its own
intrinsic frequency </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and phase </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i(t)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
Downward synchronization imposes phase coherence across depth‚Äîaligning
superficial, granular, and deep layers‚Äîwhile lateral synchronization couples
neighboring columns through horizontal fibers and axonal vector fields
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
The ensemble of these interactions produces nested oscillations that scale
naturally into the canonical neurophysiological rhythms.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Theta‚ÄìGamma Nesting.}
Theta oscillations (4‚Äì8</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>Hz) correspond to low-frequency modulations of the
scalar potential </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>‚Äîthe slow entropic envelope controlling attention and
context integration.  
Gamma oscillations (30‚Äì80</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>Hz) reflect rapid local vector fluxes
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>‚Äîthe fine-grained matching of features within a single column.
When columns synchronize their amplitwistor operations, gamma-phase packets
align within specific phases of the theta envelope:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>(t) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 + A</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sin</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span> t),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}(t) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 + A</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sin</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span> t + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
This produces phase‚Äìamplitude coupling (PAC), where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a
harmonic multiple of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, a known electrophysiological marker of
semantic binding and working-memory maintenance.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Alpha Modulation and Vector Inhibition.}
Alpha rhythms (8‚Äì12</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>Hz) represent global gating of information flow by
periodic modulation of vector divergence:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}(t) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\propto</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sin</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span> t),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
periodically suppressing or releasing local gamma activity.  
This mechanism enforces spatial segmentation, preventing destructive
interference between distinct recognition streams‚Äîanalogous to the hepatic
operator </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> enforcing equilibrium across the
plenum.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Beta and Cross-Regional Coherence.}
Beta-band oscillations (13‚Äì30</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>Hz) emerge from inter-areal synchronization of
amplitwistors across folded cortical fields.  
These oscillations correspond to torsion-minimization between distant regions,
propagating along long-range </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> tracts linking posterior and
anterior networks.  
The same formalism applies to semantic integration during language processing,
where temporo-frontal coherence reflects the recursive alignment of predicate
and argument manifolds in RRG terms.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Empirical Prediction.}
The RSVP‚ÄìCLIO model predicts that the global coherence function
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}(t) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i(t) e</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\theta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i(t)}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
should exhibit nested cross-frequency structure, where phase‚Äìamplitude
correlations scale logarithmically with cortical column density and local
curvature.  
Regions with greater folding (higher surface-to-volume ratio) should show
enhanced theta‚Äìgamma nesting and reduced entropy </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S(t)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> during recognition
tasks‚Äîa prediction directly testable with high-resolution MEG and
laminar-resolved EEG.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Integration.}
Thus, the microscopic synchronization of amplitwistors and the macroscopic
cross-frequency coupling of the cortex are the same phenomenon at different
scales: the recursive relaxation of torsion in the entropic plenum.
The cortex folds to increase the number of coupled oscillators; CLIO models
their recursive adjustment in reasoning; and EEG/MEG reveals their collective
field coherence.  
Recognition‚Äîfrom cellular resonance to conscious thought‚Äîis one continuous
