The reduction of $\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{recog}}$ is equivalent to the construction of meaning. As entropy decreases, the correlation between distributed patoms increases, forming a stable configuration that can be reactivated later as memory. Each equilibrium pattern thus encodes both recognition and prediction: recognition of the present state, and prediction of similar future configurations. In this sense, meaning is a low-entropy invariant in the cognitive field, and Patom Theory‚Äôs pattern matching constitutes a discrete manifestation of RSVP‚Äôs universal tendency toward entropic coherence.

