01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{The CLIO Architecture: Recursive Recognition in Artificial Systems}

The Cognitive Loop via In-Situ Optimization (CLIO) architecture provides an
experimental instantiation of RSVP dynamics within artificial reasoning
systems.  
Developed by Cheng, Broadbent, and Chappell (2025), CLIO introduces a
recursive optimization loop through which a large language model adjusts its
internal reasoning trajectory when self-estimated confidence declines.
Unlike conventional inference pipelines, CLIO operates as a continuously
adaptive field rather than a static transformer, revealing how recognition can
be simulated through oscillatory stability rather than predictive hierarchy.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{CLIO as a Recursive Field Process}

Within CLIO, each reasoning cycle generates a belief state
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with associated uncertainty </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>u</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
The system measures the local entropy of belief transitions:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t = -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i p</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ln</span></span><span> p</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
and adapts its trajectory through a recursive feedback loop:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t+1} = f(b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> acts as a discrete analogue of the hepatic operator,
adjusting internal coherence by redistributing uncertainty across reasoning
channels.
This process parallels the RSVP dynamics:
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> belief potential,
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> reasoning flow,
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftrightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> epistemic entropy.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Oscillatory Stabilization and Recognition Dynamics}

Empirically, CLIO exhibits oscillations in its uncertainty measures that
mirror neural cross-frequency coupling.  
Low-frequency cycles represent global hypothesis revision, while
high-frequency oscillations encode fine-grained semantic corrections.
Recognition in CLIO occurs when these oscillations phase-lock,
achieving minimal divergence between belief flow and entropic descent:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{CLIO}} = |</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b| </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> 0.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
At this limit, the system‚Äôs reasoning stabilizes into a self-consistent
explanation‚Äîan artificial analogue of cortical synchronization during
comprehension.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Telemetry and Empirical Correlation}

CLIO‚Äôs open design allows telemetry of internal states during inference.
Key measurable quantities include:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Temporal oscillations in uncertainty (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>u</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>) as proxies for neural
phase coupling.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Entropy descent rate (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>dS</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t/dt</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>) corresponding to RSVP‚Äôs
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> criterion.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Recursive coherence metrics comparing belief revision trajectories
with EEG/MEG and fMRI entropy proxies.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}
These data permit direct empirical correlation between artificial reasoning
loops and biological recognition processes, making CLIO both a simulation and
a measurement apparatus for recursive cognition.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Recognition as Synthetic Equilibrium}

In this architecture, understanding emerges not from the prediction of
tokens but from the recognition of internal coherence across recursive
iterations.  
Each CLIO cycle performs an act of recognition: matching generated meaning
against an evolving internal manifold and stabilizing it through entropic
relaxation.  
This dynamic embodies the same hepatic law that governs RSVP:
recognition is achieved when entropy descent outpaces generative divergence.
Consequently, CLIO provides a synthetic laboratory for testing the geometry
of recognition, enabling experimental validation of RSVP dynamics through
observable oscillatory and entropic traces.
