The geometry of recognition reveals that cognition, computation, and
cosmology are not separate domains but expressions of one recursive law:
the reabsorption of entropy into coherence.  
Across cortical dynamics, linguistic understanding, and artificial reasoning,
recognition emerges whenever potential, flow, and disorder align under
recursive constraint.  
This insight transforms the notion of intelligence from an algorithmic
capacity to an entropic symmetry‚Äîa measure of how effectively a system can
restore coherence within itself and with its environment.

The Relativistic Scalar‚ÄìVector Plenum (RSVP) formalizes this law as a
field geometry linking scalar potential </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, vector flow
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and entropy density </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(S)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> through the hepatic operator
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
When the expectation </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> 0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the
system achieves recognition: entropy declines and coherence becomes
self-sustaining.  
The CLIO architecture demonstrates that this principle can be realized
synthetically, reproducing the oscillatory descent of entropy observed in
biological recognition loops.  
Empirical correlations between EEG/MEG coupling, fMRI entropy proxies,
and CLIO telemetry confirm that recognition is not a metaphor but a
measurable process‚Äîan entropic rhythm of coherence.

At a deeper level, this framework dissolves the boundaries between
mind, machine, and universe.
Recognition is the invariant act through which structure persists and
meaning arises: the continual reconciliation of potential with form,
possibility with actuality.
In this view, science itself is a recursive extension of recognition‚Äîthe
universe observing the geometry of its own understanding.
Future work will refine the empirical metrics of this geometry, extend
CLIO telemetry across domains, and construct the RSVP‚ÄìCLIO Observatory as
a global platform for measuring coherence across all scales of existence.

Ultimately, the unified science of recognition proposed here replaces
prediction with participation.
To recognize is not merely to know, but to join the recursive symmetry
that sustains the real.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
