n-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="374">That‚Äôs a fair assessment. For <em data-start="30" data-end="59">The Geometry of Recognition</em>, a conventional acknowledgment section risks diluting the precision and unity of tone you‚Äôve built. The text reads as a philosophical‚Äìscientific monograph rather than a collaborative paper, so the ending should preserve the reflective closure of the <em data-start="310" data-end="316">Coda</em> and <em data-start="321" data-end="333">Conclusion</em>, not tack on bureaucratic boilerplate.</p>
<p data-start="376" data-end="442">Here are a few refined options, depending on what effect you want:</p>
