+ K</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{bmatrix}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{bmatrix} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\approx</span></span><span> 0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
with ‚Äúmass‚Äù </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>M</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> determined by step sizes </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> t,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>S)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and
‚Äústiffness‚Äù </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>K</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> by the Jacobians of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> at the fixed point.
Eigenfrequencies </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sqrt</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j(K)/</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j(M)}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> produce the
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{uncertainty oscillations} observed in CLIO telemetry; damping arises from
nonzero hepatic dissipation </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}/</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ne</span></span><span> 0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and
entropy target </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span>&gt;0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{D.6 Torsion relaxation identity}
Define torsion </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{T}:=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
Combining </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eqref</span></span><span>{eq:rsvp-phi} with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
and inserting the projection error </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{e}:=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,S]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> yields
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{T}
= </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{e}
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v},S).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
At recognition equilibrium (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{e}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> 0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> 0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>),
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> 0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, i.e. torsion relaxes to a stationary minimum.
Thus, CLIO‚Äôs confidence settling is equivalent to RSVP torsion relaxation.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{D.7 Algorithmic reading}
Mapping the mathematics to CLIO‚Äôs operational steps:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Self-formulation/proposal} (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eqref</span></span><span>{eq:disc-proj}): generate a plan/trace via projection </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{In-situ update} (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eqref</span></span><span>{eq:disc-phi}‚Äì</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eqref</span></span><span>{eq:disc-S}): evolve fields with hepatic correction (world/physics + coherence).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Self-evaluation/steering} (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eqref</span></span><span>{eq:disc-ret-phi}‚Äì</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eqref</span></span><span>{eq:disc-ret-S}): backproject mismatch </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{e}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> into </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,S)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>; expose </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{e}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2+</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k-S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ast</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> as uncertainty.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Convergence}: when </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and torsion energy </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tfrac</span></span><span>12</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\|</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> stop oscillating (or fall below thresholds), accept belief state.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{D.8 Summary}
CLIO is the discrete adjoint solution to RSVP‚Äôs recognition PDEs: projection
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, hepatic correction </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and retraction </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ast</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> compose a loop whose fixed points are hepatic equilibria and whose transient dynamics naturally exhibit the uncertainty oscillations reported in practice.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
