Role and Reference Grammar provides a linguistic formalism that mirrors this projection structure. In RRG, syntax is derived from underlying logical structures composed of semantic roles (\textit{Actor}, \textit{Undergoer}) and logical relations (\textit{predicate}, \textit{argument}). The mapping from these semantic structures to syntactic constructions is governed by linking rules that preserve meaning across layers of representation. Formally, RRG‚Äôs linking algorithm can be expressed as
