<hr data-start="2803" data-end="2806">
<h3 data-start="2808" data-end="2858">(e) <strong data-start="2816" data-end="2858">Philosophical Synthesis / Epistemology</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2859" data-end="3211">
<li data-start="2859" data-end="3047">
<p data-start="2861" data-end="3047">The philosophical implications are robust but could benefit from an explicit connection to classical epistemology (Kant, Merleau-Ponty, Gibson, Husserl) and perhaps to modern enactivism.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3048" data-end="3211">
<p data-start="3050" data-end="3211">Suggest adding a paragraph on <em data-start="3080" data-end="3108">phenomenological resonance</em> or <em data-start="3112" data-end="3128">direct realism</em>, reinforcing that recognition-first cognition implies <strong data-start="3183" data-end="3210">no representational gap</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3213" data-end="3236"><strong data-start="3213" data-end="3236">Add (‚âà1 paragraph):</strong></p>
<blockquote data-start="3237" data-end="3588">
<p data-start="3239" data-end="3588">This recognition-based epistemology aligns with the enactive and phenomenological traditions of Varela and Merleau-Ponty, for whom perception and world co-emerge through reciprocal enactment. The RSVP manifold thus formalizes what phenomenology described qualitatively: cognition as the continuous re-embedding of the perceiver within the perceived.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="3590" data-end="3593">
<h3 data-start="3595" data-end="3652">(f) <strong data-start="3603" data-end="3652">Comparative Discussion with Predictive Coding</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="3653" data-end="4202">
<li data-start="3653" data-end="4202">
<p data-start="3655" data-end="3773">You already critique predictive coding, but you can strengthen this by showing how RSVP mathematically generalizes it.</p>
<ul data-start="3776" data-end="4134">
<li data-start="3776" data-end="3905">
<p data-start="3778" data-end="3905">E.g., free energy principle corresponds to minimizing a scalar potential; RSVP adds a vector torsion term, making it symmetric.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3908" data-end="4134">
<p data-start="3910" data-end="3939">Include one explicit mapping:</p>
